Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.58,0:00:17.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If the Minister can really cause miracles with his Philosopher's Stone,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.96,0:00:20.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,then why did it turn out like this?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.66,0:00:22.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please cease fighting!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.57,0:00:25.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please cease fighting!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.84,0:00:28.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Send out the Minister!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.61,0:00:28.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Please cease fighting!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.48,0:00:30.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give us the Minister!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.99,0:00:47.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, is it okay that \Nwe're not fighting?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.61,0:00:50.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Against whom?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.27,0:00:56.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How foolish.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.13,0:01:00.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Humans are foolish beyond saving.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.06,0:01:01.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Foolish! Foolish!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.85,0:01:06.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With things going this well, \Nsuch foolishness is refreshing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.83,0:01:10.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well, well, if it isn't \Nthe almighty Minister.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.25,0:01:11.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Almighty!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.59,0:01:15.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All I did was incite the \Nmembers of the order,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.26,0:01:17.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and the believers \Nbegan killing each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.78,0:01:21.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And the military is just adding fuel to \Nthe fire by trying to quell the disorder.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.41,0:01:25.81,Dialogue,,20,20,0,,No matter how many times they repeat themselves, \Nthey never know enough to learn.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.32,0:01:28.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Humans are foolish, \Nmiserable creatures.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.88,0:01:32.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All of this to create \Na Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.82,0:01:34.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And now, I can finally...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.52,0:01:44.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,return to this adorable form.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.00,0:01:47.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That again? You enjoy making yourself up as young, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.63,0:01:51.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What else can I do? I've forgotten \Nwhat I originally looked like, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.92,0:01:57.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wh-What's going on here? \NThe Minister...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.74,0:02:00.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What have you done with the real Minister?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.15,0:02:01.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do we do?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.24,0:02:04.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't we just tell him the truth? The Minister has long since—
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.96,0:02:06.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can I eat him?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.91,0:02:22.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.61,0:02:27.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.90,0:02:32.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.64,0:02:38.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.58,0:04:17.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Come to mention it,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.42,0:04:21.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I got some information saying \Nthat guy is headed from Central to East.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.73,0:04:24.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean the State Alchemist killer?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:24.86,0:04:27.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Flame Colonel is in East City, along with...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.92,0:04:31.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By now, the Fullmetal pipsqueak is making his stay there.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.84,0:04:34.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.59,0:04:36.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.25,0:04:40.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that boy is the closest one \Nto our goal.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.66,0:04:44.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't have that guy \Njust going around on his own.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.78,0:04:47.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lust, that was delicious!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.36,0:04:50.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wipe your mouth, Gluttony.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.01,0:04:51.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right, right...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.93,0:04:55.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, what was this guy named?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.92,0:04:57.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"Scar"?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.58,0:04:58.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The scarred man?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.90,0:05:01.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't know his \Nreal identity, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.28,0:05:04.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've got eyewitness testimony saying he has a large scar on his forehead,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.99,0:05:06.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so that's what we call him.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.59,0:05:11.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And he's the one who killed a number of State Alchemists in Central?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.56,0:05:13.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nine of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.11,0:05:15.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Four just in Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.93,0:05:17.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you count the whole country,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:17.74,0:05:21.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,nine State Alchemists \Nhave fallen by his hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.88,0:05:24.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you include other \Npersonnel around them,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.44,0:05:26.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it's well into the dozens.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.81,0:05:29.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Judging from the wounds, it looks like \Nthey blew up from the inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.96,0:05:33.52,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,As far as his weapons and his objectives go, \Nwe don't know a thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.88,0:05:37.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And so, the folks at the Central Command Center panicked.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.05,0:05:40.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They made the excuse that \Nthey were escorting the Führer
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.43,0:05:42.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and went on this trip {\i1}en masse{\i0}, then?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.44,0:05:45.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So the killer won't come to this backwoods place, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.44,0:05:46.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're here, and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.18,0:05:51.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those who demoted you \Nthree years ago are aware...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.46,0:05:54.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,of your abilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.78,0:05:58.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now I'm beginning to \Nwant to run away too.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.16,0:06:01.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The issue is who \Nhis next target will be.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.85,0:06:03.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Pardon me...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.10,0:06:06.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, sorry, but I have a cute little daughter who's about to turn three—
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.30,0:06:07.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Telephone for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.51,0:06:10.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.67,0:06:12.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, hello, this is Hughes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.35,0:06:14.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.58,0:06:16.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.81,0:06:21.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The body of one of the soldiers patrolling East City Station has been found.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.20,0:06:24.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Blown up from the inside?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.45,0:06:37.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Doctor Marcoh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.05,0:06:38.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean Mauro-sensei?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.98,0:06:40.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, {\i1}Marcoh{\i0}.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.60,0:06:44.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But there's only one doctor in this village, \Nand that's Mauro-sensei.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.55,0:06:47.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As you can see, the folks along this road are poor,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.92,0:06:53.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and we had to take half a day \Njust to get to East City to see a doctor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.23,0:06:54.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's a nice fellow.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.74,0:06:59.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He'll make sure to see even patients who were given up on as incurable elsewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.27,0:07:02.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When I got my leg caught under a tractor and it looked like I was going to die,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.86,0:07:04.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he fixed me up just right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.96,0:07:07.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When he was treating him, right? There was this flash of light!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.85,0:07:09.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right, right!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.11,0:07:14.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Light...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.78,0:07:17.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's alchemy all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.19,0:07:18.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Doctor Marcoh.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.79,0:07:21.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But he's on the run \Nfrom the military, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.46,0:07:24.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why would he become a doctor? There'd be stories about him.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.30,0:07:32.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is awful! \NI'm getting straw inside me!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.31,0:07:37.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.75,0:07:39.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's a State Alchemist—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.48,0:07:42.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,one of those who was with the Führer when they came from Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.69,0:07:44.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But why is he here?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.58,0:07:46.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Did he follow us?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.65,0:07:51.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Colonel said he never reported Marcoh's whereabouts to Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.35,0:08:00.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's hurry! Marcoh's house should be close by.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.26,0:08:11.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,H-Hold on! We just wanted...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.73,0:08:15.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A State Alchemist, you say?! \NHave you come to take me back?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.84,0:08:19.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Er, you're the Crystal Alchemist, Doctor Marcoh-san, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.85,0:08:23.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want to go back there! Please! I couldn't stand that!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.77,0:08:25.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not like that! Hear us out!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.60,0:08:27.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Look, that's dangerous!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.77,0:08:29.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or have you come to silence me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.38,0:08:33.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You think you can kill me? I... I...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.99,0:08:36.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.24,0:08:39.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.58,0:08:43.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even if you kill me, I won't die.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.46,0:08:57.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.40,0:09:01.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see, you're the Fullmetal Alchemist...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.60,0:09:07.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}No, that would be me! \NI'm him, actually.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.86,0:09:20.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I deserted the battlefield,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.03,0:09:24.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and when I did, I stole the research materials that I had at the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.92,0:09:28.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The military is probably \Nstill after those materials.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.88,0:09:30.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's it!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.21,0:09:34.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The truth is, we're looking into human transmutation—
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.02,0:09:35.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.85,0:09:37.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,show you anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.69,0:09:43.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Orders from above notwithstanding, \NI stained my hands with that research.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.32,0:09:47.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And then, it was used in the \Nmassacre of the Eastern Rebellion.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.30,0:09:50.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Massacre?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.66,0:09:52.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean the uprising at Ishbal?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.69,0:09:54.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was terrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.52,0:09:57.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was a truly terrible battle.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.91,0:10:00.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Children... women...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.48,0:10:02.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They were all killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.74,0:10:04.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There was no justifiable reason for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.62,0:10:08.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was reason enough that they were the people of Ishbal and defied the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.00,0:10:14.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I could never fully make up for what \NI did there even if I gave up my own life.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.24,0:10:20.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even so, I decided to do all that I can, which is why I am a doctor here.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.82,0:10:24.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go back.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.63,0:10:29.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm a State Alchemist! \NI have a right to see your research!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.38,0:10:31.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As little as you are?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.12,0:10:34.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll bet you were blinded by \Nthe abundant research funding
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.46,0:10:37.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and numerous privileges, \Nso you got yourself certified.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.31,0:10:39.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What foolishness.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.66,0:10:41.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you were there during \Nthe rebellion, you would also—
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.88,0:10:43.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.28,0:10:47.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know what we're doing is stupid. But even so...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.38,0:10:52.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.18,0:10:57.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,About five years ago, you treated \Nthe babies at Xenotime, didn't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.29,0:11:01.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The babies from that time are now doing fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.27,0:11:08.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.35,0:11:14.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No transmutation circle?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.97,0:11:20.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is this the red water of Xenotime? \NNo, this appears to be much clearer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.28,0:11:22.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.00,0:11:22.21,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.32,0:11:24.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, this is wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.20,0:11:26.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let go of me!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.28,0:11:27.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.24,0:11:29.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let go of me, I said!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.62,0:11:36.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not a liquid?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:36.95,0:11:38.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, it...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.06,0:11:41.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It looks like that thing that the Minister at Liore had.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.90,0:11:49.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Sage's Stone, the Celestial Stone...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.65,0:11:53.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Great Elixir, the Red Tincture, the Fifth Element...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.88,0:11:56.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just as it is called by many names,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.89,0:11:59.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,its form is also not limited to that of a stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.74,0:12:01.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brigadier General Grand...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.86,0:12:03.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brigadier General?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.65,0:12:06.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My, you've moved up in the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.40,0:12:11.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Crystal Alchemist,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.02,0:12:14.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,you will turn over the Philosopher's Stone, along with all of your materials.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.03,0:12:17.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Philosopher's Stone?! That?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.23,0:12:21.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At best, it is an experimentally produced item.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.43,0:12:24.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no telling when it will \Nreach its limit and become unusable.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.08,0:12:29.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's an unstable, defective product, \Nand it's different from the genuine article.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.12,0:12:32.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But during the rebellion, \Nit did augment our abilities,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.99,0:12:35.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and we displayed tremendous power!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.18,0:12:51.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, are you saying \Nthat in the past,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.80,0:12:54.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the military researched \Nthe Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.46,0:12:58.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Never mind that it isn't perfect. \NIf that was made by human hands...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.99,0:13:02.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it means that it's possible to \Ncreate a Philosopher's Stone as well!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.64,0:13:04.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where is the manufacturing technique?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.48,0:13:09.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you mean to do \Nonce you see it, Fullmetal Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:10.42,0:13:14.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The research is top secret \Nand falls under my jurisdiction.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.21,0:13:16.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I cannot permit you \Nto see the materials.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.16,0:13:18.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.39,0:13:24.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,L-Let go of me! No! No!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.20,0:13:28.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please don't! Forgive me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.46,0:13:30.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want to go back there!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.45,0:13:32.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't want to go back!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.90,0:13:35.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've had enough of it! \NPlease forgive me!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.75,0:13:37.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't stand it!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.42,0:13:39.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't stand anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.44,0:13:41.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's just like that other time...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.18,0:13:53.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.62,0:13:58.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I may not have grown at all,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.26,0:14:02.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I can't let my heart stay stunted!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.06,0:14:23.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.97,0:14:27.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Iron Blood Alchemist, Basque Grand...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.71,0:14:31.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Too bad for you!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.43,0:14:34.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I now have this!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.60,0:14:40.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.20,0:14:54.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.70,0:14:57.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's the guy I saw three years ago \Nin Central. I'm sure of it...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.41,0:15:01.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Never mind that! This is bad!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.03,0:15:03.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My instincts are telling me to run,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.58,0:15:05.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but my legs won't move!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.38,0:15:13.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Crystal Alchemist, Doctor Marcoh...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.10,0:15:15.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard that you were dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.01,0:15:19.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I must take special care...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.02,0:15:21.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,to kill you!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.65,0:15:22.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.58,0:15:26.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see. This must be fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.41,0:15:31.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In the name of God, \Nthou shalt perish!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.37,0:15:36.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-kun!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.72,0:15:39.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you giving up for?! Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.25,0:15:41.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fullmetal Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.80,0:15:43.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You will not escape either!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.33,0:15:47.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He knows me? \NWhat's going on here?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.56,0:15:50.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've done plenty of stuff \Nto get people mad at me,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.14,0:15:53.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}but I've never given anyone \Na reason to come after my life!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.00,0:15:59.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, this way!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.09,0:16:38.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.00,0:16:39.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you after us?!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.88,0:16:43.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you are creators, then there must also be a destroyer.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.46,0:16:47.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Edward-kun, leave me behind and run!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.44,0:16:57.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You have a fine look in your eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.70,0:17:00.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My older brother also had the same look in his eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.43,0:17:07.73,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Eyes that were strong, that peered far away \Ninto the endless distance...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.01,0:17:13.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Three years ago, was it?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.13,0:17:17.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I was glad to hear that you had \Ngiven up being a State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.80,0:17:21.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's too bad. However!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.89,0:17:24.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Too slow!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.19,0:17:27.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.23,0:17:37.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.78,0:17:39.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Make no mistake.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.64,0:17:44.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I meant to destroy a human body, \Nso you got away with just that crack.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.61,0:17:46.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stay out of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.52,0:17:49.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My only enemy is the State Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.88,0:17:52.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:52.50,0:17:54.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you after us?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.21,0:17:57.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemists are those who take things \Nfrom their natural form
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.44,0:18:00.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and transform them into something grotesque.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.40,0:18:05.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is to say, they profane God, the creator of all things.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.73,0:18:09.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As an agent of God,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.04,0:18:11.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am he who hands down his judgment.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.38,0:18:18.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm an alchemist too! \NI may not have the state's certification...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.14,0:18:20.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why do you wish to die?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.71,0:18:24.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mentioned your older brother a moment ago, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.48,0:18:26.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then you should understand!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.84,0:18:30.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no way anyone could watch their brother get killed.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.00,0:18:32.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Even you—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.84,0:18:32.92,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,I do understand!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.45,0:18:38.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The way I felt when I had to watch as \Nmy brother was killed before my eyes...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.48,0:18:41.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is exactly...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.50,0:18:42.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,why I must now...!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.10,0:18:48.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I told you, you're too slow.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.16,0:19:00.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Automail?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.41,0:19:04.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So your right arm brings forth \Nnothing but destruction as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.62,0:19:08.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't go lumping my \Nright arm in with yours!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.96,0:19:26.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A State Alchemist?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.63,0:19:29.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you here to take Marcoh-san?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.89,0:19:41.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry I'm late. I was assigned by the Lt. Colonel to guard you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.52,0:19:43.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By Lt. Colonel Hughes?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.02,0:19:50.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Agent of God, you say? In that case, try passing judgment upon me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.56,0:19:53.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For I am the Strong Arm Alchemist,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.83,0:19:56.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alex Louis Armstrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.72,0:20:01.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What a fine day this is!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.50,0:20:04.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That you would come forward \Nand save me the trouble of finding you...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.73,0:20:07.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Could this be the grace of God?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.68,0:20:09.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Allow me to show you \Nthe artistic alchemy
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.40,0:20:14.86,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that has been passed down among \Nthe Armstrong family for generations!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:19.65,0:20:21.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Another shot!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.06,0:20:30.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As you can see, \Nthere are only children here!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.60,0:20:33.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There aren't any of the guerillas you're looking for!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.66,0:20:39.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does this mean you've abandoned \Nthe so-called teachings of Cornello?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:39.42,0:20:40.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.85,0:20:44.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tell us the location of the faction that's resisting military rule!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.62,0:20:45.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.04,0:20:53.06,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,We came to liberate this town from Cornello! \NDon't you understand?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.72,0:20:57.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This town is our home.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.80,0:20:59.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to move forward,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.66,0:21:02.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,even if it's only a little at a time, under our own power.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.80,0:21:05.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our legs are fine, after all!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.16,0:21:23.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You dropped this.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.62,0:21:31.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You didn't think about \Nrunning away with this?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.12,0:21:35.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You used it to treat people in that clinic, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.26,0:21:41.61,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,I can't forget the looks on the faces of \Nthose people who told us about you today.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.40,0:21:49.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That belongs to those people, and so do you.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.84,0:21:52.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can you walk?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.12,0:21:55.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, let's go.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.81,0:21:59.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Someplace where neither that guy nor the military will follow us.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.98,0:22:01.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can we escape them?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.31,0:22:06.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You still have your legs, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.62,0:23:40.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.22,0:23:43.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 15: "The Ishbal Massacre"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.77,0:23:46.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We don't know anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:47.61,0:23:51.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But you can't use ignorance as an excuse to absolve yourself.
